menu "Home Assistant TFT dashboard firmware"

choice HA_PANEL
    prompt "Which display panel is physically connected"
    default HA_PANEL_D320C2403V1_JD9168
    help
        The panel abstraction (main/ha_panel.h) is a hard requirement of this
        firmware so more panels can be added later without touching anything
        else - main.c, ha_lvgl.c and ha_dashboard.c only ever call the
        ha_panel_*()/ha_touch_*() interface, never a driver directly. Only one
        physical panel is supported today.

    config HA_PANEL_D320C2403V1_JD9168
        bool "D320C2403V1-MIPI, 1024x768, JD9168 driver, GT967 touch"
        help
            The panel examples/idf_dsi_camera_preview already proved on this
            board: 3.2", MIPI-DSI, RGB888, 2 data lanes, plugged into FPC1
            through an adapter board carrying its own TCA6408 at 0x20.
endchoice

config HA_DISPLAY_BRIGHTNESS_PERCENT
    int "Backlight brightness while awake (percent)"
    default 80
    range 5 100
    help
        Passed to ha_panel_set_backlight() once the dashboard is built. The
        backlight is the SGM37604A on the display module, driven over I2C -
        there is no PWM/GPIO brightness control on this board.

config HA_DISPLAY_DIM_PERCENT
    int "Backlight brightness after the idle timeout (percent)"
    default 15
    range 0 100
    help
        A wall panel that is always showing something bright, always, is
        both needless glare and needless backlight wear. Any touch restores
        HA_DISPLAY_BRIGHTNESS_PERCENT immediately, skipping this dimmed
        stage entirely - see HA_DISPLAY_OFF_DELAY_S for what happens if the
        panel stays untouched even longer than this.

config HA_DISPLAY_IDLE_TIMEOUT_S
    int "Seconds of no touch before dimming"
    default 120
    range 10 3600

config HA_DISPLAY_OFF_DELAY_S
    int "Further seconds of no touch (after dimming) before the backlight turns off"
    default 60
    range 5 3600
    help
        Measured from when the panel dims (HA_DISPLAY_IDLE_TIMEOUT_S), not
        from the last touch - so the total time from last touch to backlight
        off is HA_DISPLAY_IDLE_TIMEOUT_S + this value. Any touch restores
        full brightness immediately, direct from off - there is no need to
        "wake" it back through the dimmed stage first.

config HA_WS_DEFAULT_PORT
    int "Default Home Assistant WebSocket port"
    default 8123
    range 1 65535
    help
        Pre-fills the stage-2 config page's port field the first time it is
        shown. The actual value used is always whatever ends up in NVS.

config HA_WS_RECONNECT_MIN_MS
    int "Minimum reconnect backoff (ms)"
    default 1000
    range 200 60000

config HA_WS_RECONNECT_MAX_MS
    int "Maximum reconnect backoff (ms)"
    default 30000
    range 1000 300000
    help
        The Home Assistant WebSocket client (main/ha_ws.c) reconnects
        indefinitely on any disconnect - HA restarts routinely, e.g. after an
        update - doubling the backoff from the minimum up to this cap, with
        jitter, rather than spinning or waiting out one fixed interval.

endmenu
